{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence so far shows RNA (scvi_n200, multi, avgpool) is the strongest modality at 0.650 acc, while image-only (ResNet50) is very weak at 0.208. The critical open question is whether the image modality contributes complementary signal when fused with the best RNA configuration, or whether it is purely noise that degrades performance. Config_030 (multimodal, multi, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests this by pairing the strongest RNA setup with the weakest image encoder under the simplest fusion (concat). If accuracy exceeds 0.650, multimodal fusion is worth further exploration (ViT, weighted fusion); if it falls below, the image branch is not useful and remaining budget should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation refinements. This single experiment resolves the highest-uncertainty design decision—whether to invest in multimodal or unimodal strategies—making it the most budget-efficient next step."
}

